---
// pro.bayshine.net/about — the story behind the operator network.
// Third-person business voice, matches src/pages/about.astro convention.
// Self-contained: imports ProLayout only.
import ProLayout from '@/components/pro/ProLayout.astro';
---
<ProLayout
  title="About BayShine Operators | The story behind the network"
  description="BayShine started as one mobile detailing operation in Land O' Lakes. The methodology that built it is becoming the documented standard certified operators run under the BayShine name."
  canonical="https://pro.bayshine.net/about"
>

  <!-- ── HERO ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="noise-overlay py-24 px-4">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <div class="reveal">
        <p class="text-bay-gold text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] mb-6">
          The story behind the program
        </p>
        <h1 class="font-display font-bold text-4xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl text-bay-white leading-[1.08] mb-8 tracking-tight" style="text-shadow: 0 2px 24px rgba(15,27,45,0.7);">
          Solo operation.<br />Documented standard.<br />Becoming a network.
        </h1>
        <p class="text-bay-bone text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
          BayShine started as one mobile detailing operation in Land O' Lakes,
          Florida. The methodology that built it is now becoming the standard a
          certified operator can run anywhere the brand goes.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider" />

  <!-- ── WHERE IT STARTED ───────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="py-20 px-4">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <div class="reveal">
        <p class="text-bay-gold text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] mb-4">Where it started</p>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-3xl text-bay-white mb-8 leading-tight">
          Pasco County. One technician. One market.
        </h2>

        <p class="text-bay-bone text-base leading-relaxed mb-6">
          BayShine began as a single mobile operation serving Land O' Lakes and the
          surrounding Pasco County and North Hillsborough corridor. The market was
          full of operators treating detailing as a commodity: high volume, low
          attention, identical results regardless of what the vehicle actually needed.
          The work here ran opposite from the start.
        </p>

        <p class="text-bay-bone text-base leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Mobile was the obvious format. Fewer overheads kept the rate competitive.
          Working at the client's location meant the vehicle did not sit in a lot
          between stages. Every appointment was a single vehicle and a fixed
          chemical and mechanical sequence. Nothing was rushed because the sequence
          was the product.
        </p>

        <p class="text-bay-slate text-sm leading-relaxed">
          More on the operating philosophy on the main site:
          <a href="https://bayshine.net/about" class="text-bay-gold hover:text-[#d9bc79] underline underline-offset-4 transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-bay-gold rounded-sm">bayshine.net/about</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider" />

  <!-- ── METHODOLOGY BECAME IP ─────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="noise-overlay section-bevel bg-bay-deep py-20 px-4">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <div class="reveal">
        <p class="text-bay-gold text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] mb-4">The methodology became the IP</p>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-3xl text-bay-white mb-8 leading-tight">
          The sequence is the product.
        </h2>

        <p class="text-bay-bone text-base leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Every exterior service at BayShine runs through a fixed sequence: iron
          decontamination first to lift embedded brake dust at the chemistry level
          before any mechanical contact, synthetic clay second to mechanically pull
          surface-bonded contamination that chemistry alone will not move, two-stage
          hand wash, then polymer sealant on a surface that is genuinely clean.
          Sealing contaminated paint protects the contamination, not the paint.
          That order does not move.
        </p>

        <p class="text-bay-bone text-base leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Interior work follows the same logic: compressed air and vacuum before
          any surface contact to prevent grinding debris into fabric or trim,
          agitation before extraction, enzymatic odor treatment that neutralizes
          rather than masks.
        </p>

        <p class="text-bay-bone text-base leading-relaxed">
          What started as one technician's practice has been documented job by
          job. Every visit refines the checklist. That documentation is what gets
          handed to certified operators, along with the training to run it to
          standard. A BayShine detail in Lutz looks the same as a BayShine detail
          in Wesley Chapel because the sequence does the work.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider" />

  <!-- ── WHY A NETWORK ─────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="py-20 px-4">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <div class="reveal">
        <p class="text-bay-gold text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] mb-4">Why a network now</p>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-3xl text-bay-white mb-8 leading-tight">
          The good operator is rare. So is the customer who can find one.
        </h2>

        <p class="text-bay-bone text-base leading-relaxed mb-6">
          The detailer who actually cares about the work is uncommon in this
          market. They are usually solo. They are usually marketing themselves,
          fighting for their own bookings, while the operators who do not care
          take the bulk of the volume by being louder. Their customer side faces
          the mirror image: most ways to find a detailer give the customer no real
          way to tell who will do the job right and who will hit a volume target
          and call it finished.
        </p>

        <p class="text-bay-bone text-base leading-relaxed mb-6">
          A brand that operates to a documented standard solves both ends of that
          problem. The customer pays for predictability and gets it. The operator
          gets the bookings they earn through the work, without spending their
          weekends running ads or chasing leads that never close.
        </p>

        <p class="text-bay-bone text-base leading-relaxed">
          BayShine Operators is that brand made portable.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider" />

  <!-- ── WHAT WE'RE BUILDING TOWARD ────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="noise-overlay section-bevel bg-bay-deep py-20 px-4">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <div class="reveal">
        <p class="text-bay-gold text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] mb-4">What we are building toward</p>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-3xl text-bay-white mb-8 leading-tight">
          A network of certified mobile detailers running the same standard.
        </h2>

        <p class="text-bay-bone text-base leading-relaxed mb-6">
          The plan is direct: a certified operator network running the BayShine
          standard, starting in Pasco County and North Hillsborough and expanding
          through Florida as the operator roster grows. Every operator runs the
          same checklist. Every customer sees the same standard. The brand
          carries the recognition. The operator brings the craft.
        </p>

        <p class="text-bay-bone text-base leading-relaxed mb-6">
          The first wave is small, hand-picked, and trained against the documented
          standard in-market. First-wave operators become reference operators for
          the next intake. The trade is honest: early access in exchange for
          being part of how the standard gets refined.
        </p>

        <p class="text-bay-bone text-base leading-relaxed">
          The economics, the legal structure, and the territory model will evolve
          as the operator network grows. The standard does not.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider" />

  <!-- ── WHAT THIS IS NOT ─────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="py-20 px-4">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <div class="reveal">
        <p class="text-bay-gold text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] mb-4">What this is not</p>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-3xl text-bay-white mb-8 leading-tight">
          Honest about what BayShine Operators is, and is not.
        </h2>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="border-l-2 border-bay-gold pl-5">
            <p class="font-display font-semibold text-bay-white text-base mb-2">Not a franchise sale.</p>
            <p class="text-bay-slate text-sm leading-relaxed">
              No upfront fee, no territory purchase, no royalty schedule. The
              first-wave structure is direct: get certified, run jobs, get paid a
              percentage. The legal structure will mature as the network grows, and
              that maturation will be openly discussed with the operators it affects.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="border-l-2 border-bay-gold pl-5">
            <p class="font-display font-semibold text-bay-white text-base mb-2">Not a lead-gen marketplace.</p>
            <p class="text-bay-slate text-sm leading-relaxed">
              BayShine does not sell the same job to three operators and let them
              fight over it. Each job routes to one certified operator based on
              location and certification tier. The job is theirs to run.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="border-l-2 border-bay-gold pl-5">
            <p class="font-display font-semibold text-bay-white text-base mb-2">Not a chain hiring warm bodies.</p>
            <p class="text-bay-slate text-sm leading-relaxed">
              The certification is the gate. Operators who will not run the
              sequence to standard do not get the shirt. That is the entire
              product BayShine is selling to the customer; compromising it
              compromises everything.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider" />

  <!-- ── FINAL CTA ──────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="noise-overlay bg-bay-deep py-20 px-4">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
      <div class="reveal">
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-bay-white mb-4">
          First-wave applications are open.
        </h2>
        <p class="text-bay-slate mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          Pasco County and North Hillsborough. Small group, direct conversation,
          documented standard.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/#apply"
          class="btn-sweep gloss-cap bg-bay-gold text-bay-navy font-semibold text-base px-8 py-3.5 rounded-sm hover:bg-[#d9bc79] transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-bay-gold focus-visible:ring-offset-2 focus-visible:ring-offset-bay-deep inline-block"
        >
          Apply for the first wave
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</ProLayout>
